@startuml
title Audit finding 1 — forging a collection through the mint-before-burn hook (pre-fix code)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #B54A4A
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
  ActorBackgroundColor #FDEEEE
  ActorBorderColor #B54A4A
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A78B5
  GroupBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
  GroupBorderColor #B54A4A
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FDEEEE
  BorderColor #B54A4A
}

actor "Attacker\ncontract" as A
participant "ConditionalTokens\n(vulnerable revision)" as CT
participant "Collateral\nERC-20" as ERC20

note over A
  Under the old AdHash scheme a collection ID was
  the truncated sum of the member hashes, so the
  attacker can solve for a parent ID P such that
  splitting P lands on an already redeemable ID.
end note

A -> CT : splitPosition(collateral, P, conditionId, [0b10, 0b01], amount)
activate CT

CT -> CT : derive target position IDs
note right of CT #FDEEEE
  Old ordering: mint the targets first,
  burn the source afterwards.
end note

CT -> CT : _mint(targets)
CT -> A : onERC1155Received(...)
activate A

group Re-entrant calls, source stake not yet burnt
  A -> CT : redeemPositions(collateral, P, conditionId, [0b01])
  CT -> CT : mint stake in position P\n(so the pending burn will succeed)
  A -> CT : redeemPositions(collateral, 0, conditionId, [0b01])
  CT -> ERC20 : transfer(attacker, payout)
  note right of ERC20
    Collateral leaves the contract for a
    position that was never backed.
  end note
end

A --> CT : return onERC1155Received.selector
deactivate A

CT -> CT : _burn(position P, amount)\nsucceeds thanks to the re-entrant mint
CT --> A : PositionSplit
deactivate CT

note over CT
  Fix: burn or pull collateral BEFORE minting,
  and replace AdHash with the elliptic curve
  multiset hash so parent IDs cannot be forged.
end note
@enduml
